    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Dubai/Program-Manager--Dubai-McDonough-School-of-Business_JR26392": {
      "title": "Program Manager, International Graduate Programs | McDonough School of Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Program Manager, International Graduate Programs | McDonough School of Business - Georgetown University This role is locally based in Athens, Greece This role represents a foundation-building opportunity within the McDonough School of Business, as it will support the establishment of graduate degree program offerings in Athens, Greece, through a partnership with the Public Power Corporation (PPC), the country’s leading integrated electric utility and largest power provider. Through this partnership, Georgetown will deliver graduate education in Athens, launching the Executive Master’s in Leadership (EML) program in the 2026-2027 academic year, followed by the M.S. in Environment and Sustainability Management (ESM) program – a joint degree offering with Georgetown’s Earth Commons Institute – in the subsequent year. The programs may run in parallel or on an alternating basis, and additional programs may be introduced in future years, under an initial 10-year agreement with PPC. The Program Manager will play a pivotal role in establishing and orchestrating the student-facing elements of Georgetown programs in Greece. Key responsibilities include facilitating program operations, student services, event planning, and faculty/academic support to ensure that all facets of the degree programs are delivered with high quality, a high-touch approach, and professionalism. This level of effort may extend to off-site activities in Athens, Greece, as well as international components such as residencies or modules held abroad. The Program Manager may also be asked to travel and support program operations in Dubai, UAE – where McDonough maintains a branch campus – for any degree, custom program, or short executive education courses that may arise. The Program Manager may also be asked to provide administrative support for admissions and business development efforts (and associated staff) in Athens and the region (e.g., help arrange meetings between sponsor company representatives and Georgetown staff responsible for recruiting and business development). This position will require regular communication and collaboration with mid-career to executive students, seasoned faculty, and diverse faculty and staff across the university and different time zones, as well as external vendors and service providers. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to adapt and work well in a small, dynamic team and startup environment are essential for success in this role. Core duties include, but are not limited to: Lead day-to-day program operations for graduate degree offerings in Athens, ensuring seamless delivery of academic and student-facing activities. Coordinate and deliver high-quality student services for mid-career and executive learners. Plan and execute program-related events, residencies, and international modules, including logistics in Greece and abroad. Provide operational and administrative support to faculty, including classroom readiness. Support operations, admissions, and business development by coordinating meetings, managing logistics, and liaising with corporate partners and vendors. Work Interactions Based at the Georgetown building at 42 Kraterou Zografou, Athens, this role serves as a critical bridge between McDonough’s global hubs and a key connection between the Academic Director, faculty, and others who are largely based in Washington, DC. The role will report to the Dubai-based Director of Program Management and Academic Operations, maintaining a close partnership with the Dubai team while simultaneously collaborating with faculty and staff from McDonough’s Office of the Dean, Graduate & Executive Degree Programs, Admissions, and Finance, as well as the Earth Commons Institute, and other central offices on Georgetown’s Hilltop Campus in Washington, DC. Requirements and Qualifications BA/BS required. Professionals with 6+ years of experience in operations/program/events management.  Ability to work well with mid- to senior-level executives and faculty members, as well as a deep commitment to establishing strong relationships with students enrolled in the Athens-based degree programs. Must be capable of working efficiently with Canvas, Microsoft Office Suite, especially MS Excel, as well as the Google Suite of software. Fluency in Greek and English is required. The incumbent must reside within easy commuting distance of the Georgetown building in Athens, or be willing to relocate to within easy commuting distance of Athens at their own expense. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in higher education or a customer-centric industry (e.g. hospitality, retail, etc.) and/or familiarity with the educational landscape in Greece or the Southeastern European region is a plus. Exhibit the ability to bring a fresh and entrepreneurial perspective, creating enthusiasm around a shared vision for operational efficiency and customer service to create a solid foundation for Georgetown in Greece. Work Mode Designation This position’s work mode has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $47,586.00 - $87,558.13 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/SWQ-Parking-Garage-Parking-Level-4/Landscape-Gardener-2_JR24769-1": {
      "title": "Landscape Gardener-2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Position: Full-time: 40 hours Pay: $21.45 Location: 37th & O Street NW Washington, DC 20057 Job Overview Performs landscape gardener work by preparing and maintaining landscaped areas as part of the services provided by the Facilities Management department to maintain university buildings and grounds.  Duties include grass mowing, trimming and edging, removal of weeds and daily policing of the grounds, irrigating lawns and planted areas, mulching, reactivating flower beds and tree saucers, laying sod assisting in the application of pesticides and other related work.  Incumbent is assigned to a central landscape maintenance group and performs semi-skilled landscape labor work in accordance with industry/trade practices.  Workers perform monthly assignments according to seasonal schedules, in response to requests for service (e.g. preventive maintenance of storm drain throughout the campus) and in response to emergencies.  Incumbent use all standard tools, equipment, materials and supplies of the trade and observes all safety rules, regulations and precautions in performing their duties. Work Interactions The position reports directly to the Landscape and Grounds Supervisor along with eight other laborers Gardener II and Gardener positions. The position reports indirectly to the Gardener II or Gardener positions. The position is part of a landscape maintenance team that receives training and experience vital to the maintenance of exterior space on the campus, generally referred to as landscape maintenance. This worker supports a direct service of the department in ensuring an attractive, comfortable, safe and clean environment in which the University community can live, learn and work.   Requirements and Qualifications High School Diploma required or equivalency Requires one to three years of grounds landscape maintenance experience Requires valid driver’s license and ability to operate pickup trucks, tractors, skid steer loaders, all-terrain vehicles and other specialized grounds equipment. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
