    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Community-Director--McCarthy-Hall_JR27283": {
      "title": "Community Director, McCarthy Hall",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements The Community Director in Residential Education at Georgetown University administers the residential program for a campus community housing between 225-600 students. The Community Director’s primary role is to foster the holistic development of students through active engagement and mentoring of students in the residential education experience. Duties include supervision and development of the Resident Assistant or Resident Fellow staff and the design of cultural, educational, and social programming supporting the formation of students in the Jesuit tradition. The Community Director, in partnership with the Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow staff, educates students through the development of Educational Plans, promotion of leadership development, partnerships with Faculty and Resident Ministers, emergency response, and through community investment in an established code that emphasizes respect for self and others. The Community Director manages the occupancy, safety, and security of the residential area they oversee. The Community Director is a critical member of Georgetown’s Safety Net and works closely with the Georgetown University Police Department and other Student Affairs offices to respond to student emergencies, including mental health crises, facility emergencies, injury, and other concerns. The Community Director serves on an emergency response duty rotation and responds to significant student issues. During the summer months, Community Directors play a vital role in creating and planning departmental programs and services while supporting the residential conference and intern housing operations. Community Directors are expected to serve as positive ambassadors of the University and Residential Living mission, vision, and values within their teams, communities, and across campus. The Community Director primarily performs desk work in an office or workspace using a university issued computer. Some meetings or events occur in other buildings on the Hilltop or Capitol Campus or occasionally at off campus locations. This position is required to live on campus and participate in an on-call/on-site duty rotation 24-hours a day, 365 days a year. The Community Director must be able to respond quickly to emergencies (behavioral, health related, and facility/physical plant) and other needs when they arise. Work Interactions Community Directors supervise the student Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow team and lead all community development and student formation initiatives within their assigned community. The Community Director provides mediation services to students, supervision to Resident Assistant/Resident Fellow staff, developmental guidance to students, and feedback to departmental leadership. On a daily basis the Community Director schedules student meetings and is readily available to student staff and colleagues. The Community Director is expected to communicate in a timely manner with faculty, staff, parents, and others regarding shared concerns about students.  Requirements and Qualifications A completed Master's Degree is required, preferably in the area of Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or Social Work. Thorough understanding of and commitment to the work of Residential Living as well as the education and character development of college students is expected. Demonstrated experience in the areas of leadership, supervision, professional development, administrative skills, social justice and inclusion, community development, educational engagement, and emergency response. Ability to manage stress, conflict, and frustration constructively; demonstrate a positive attitude. Identify, define, and apply creative and original approaches to resolving issues and use sound judgment based on training and departmental policies and protocol. An awareness and understanding of the Jesuit values and the ability to conceptualize them in the application of this role. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Emergency Employee This position has been designated as an emergency position. Because many services provided by the University are required seven days a week on a twenty-four hour basis, the University makes every effort to remain open at all times. This position must always report to work on time regardless of weather conditions, whether the University is closed or not. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $41,926.00 - $65,090.00 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/ICC-2nd-Floor/Executive-Director-of-External-Relations-and-Marketing--Walsh-School-of-Foreign-Service--SFS-_JR27445": {
      "title": "Executive Director of External Relations and Marketing, Walsh School of Foreign Service (SFS)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements The Walsh School of Foreign Service (SFS), founded in 1919, is a premier school of international relations. At Georgetown’s Washington, D.C. and Qatar campuses, SFS provides a rigorous education combining theory and practice and instills the values of service.  The School's liberal arts undergraduate program, leading to the Bachelor of Science in Foreign Service, includes a two-year required core curriculum followed by two years of multidisciplinary electives. Eight interdisciplinary graduate programs are designed to teach students to think, analyze and act with imagination, good judgment and compassion.  The vision of the School is to contribute to global peace, prosperity and human well-being by educating future generations of world leaders and expanding the knowledge, understanding and values that will inform their leadership. The Executive Director of External Relations and Marketing will plan and direct a strategic and effective communications and external relations program for the School that increases stakeholder engagement and public interest in the School, and enhances the image of the School.  This will include overseeing the School’s communications and events team, and the external relations staff and outreach activities of the School.  The Executive Director will provide strategic leadership to the constituent academic units of the School on all matters relating to communications and external relations, with the aim of ensuring consistency and efficiency in the development and delivery of all communications and in engagement with stakeholders.  The Executive Director will develop and implement a strategic marketing campaign to increase applications to SFS undergraduate and graduate programs with particular attention to strengthening our international and under-represented applicant pool. The Executive Director will strengthen our outreach to the SFS alumni community including regular communications on campus happenings, fast-break analysis from SFS faculty in response to global issues, and specially tailored alumni events in key alumni markets. The Executive Director will work with SFS faculty to promote their research on areas of interest to the policy community. The Executive Director will have oversight for conceptualization and implementation of signature and/or stakeholder-focused events related to the School. The Executive Director will also engage University officials to include the Office of the GU President, Chairs, Deans and Directors on matters pertaining to communications, marketing, and event planning for the school. The Executive Director will also be expected to strengthen the School’s engagement with the broader Washington, DC policy, multilateral, and business communities ensuring topical and high-profile visits from policymakers and practitioners to campus and strategic outreach on key global issues. Reporting to the Dean, the Executive Director of External Relations and Marketing will be a member of the School's senior leadership team, participating in critical decisions and advising the Dean on important matters related to the School and the School’s role in the broader policy dialogue.  The Executive Director will play a key advisory role in developing strategies for those areas that impact the stakeholder experience.  The Executive Director supervises the School’s Director of Communications, Director of Events and Alumni Engagement, and Web Content Producer. Minimum requirements include a Bachelor’s degree in public relations, communications, marketing, higher education administration, or related field, and at least 10 years of progressively responsible experience in communications and/or external relations, preferably in higher education, government, multilateral or policy-related institutions, including 5 years of supervisory experience (or equivalent combination of education and work experience). Master’s degree preferred. A broad and up-to-date understanding of communications and external relations strategies is expected. Knowledge of the Washington DC institutional landscape is desirable. The successful candidate will have exceptional writing and presentational skills as well as demonstrated ability to organize teams to achieve results, and the ability to quickly garner credibility and develop and maintain relationships with a wide variety of internal and external stakeholders. A high level of organizational competence and effective time management is expected.  This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff and AAP positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $103,723.00 - $202,778.93 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/500-First-St-NW-7th-Floor/Temporary-People-Operations-Associate--Center-for-Security-and-Emerging-Technology--CSET---Walsh-School-of-Foreign-Service--SFS-_JR27446": {
      "title": "Temporary People Operations Associate, Center for Security and Emerging Technology (CSET), Walsh School of Foreign Service (SFS)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Center for Security and Emerging Technology (CSET), under the School of Foreign Service, is seeking applications for a temporary People Operations Associate to help expand CSET’s recruitment capacity. Reporting to CSET's People Operations Manager, the People Operations Associate will strengthen CSET’s candidate sourcing and outreach strategy and execution, take ownership of core recruiting operations, and serve as a thought partner on recruitment process improvement. The People Operations Associate will work ~25 hours each week with a compensated hourly rate of $35 per hour.  CSET is a research organization focused on studying the security impacts of emerging technologies, supporting academic work in security and technology studies, and delivering nonpartisan analysis to technologists and policymakers. CSET focuses on the frontiers of artificial intelligence, advanced computing, cyber, and biotechnology, as well as security applications, governance, and workforce for emerging technologies. CSET is located in Georgetown University’s Capitol Campus near Union Station. Members of our team are challenged with meaningful work, offered ongoing opportunities for professional development and learning, and contribute to a collegial and engaging environment where they can thrive. We are deeply committed to fostering a culture of inclusion and encourage individuals with diverse backgrounds and experiences to apply. Important Note: Please visit CSET’s career page for more detailed information on role responsibilities and application instructions. Responsibilities/Work Interactions The People Operations Associate will report to the People Operations Manager and will be responsible for: Recruiting Operations: Managing the CSET Careers general inbox, including triage, candidate correspondence, and response tracking Assisting the People Operations Manager with initial down-selection of candidates for active open roles Serving as an additional point of contact for candidates throughout the interview process Managing logistics for onsite interviews, including scheduling, interviewer coordination, candidate travel, and day-of support Sourcing and Candidate Pipeline Management: Proactively sourcing candidates for open roles via LinkedIn Recruiter, relevant job boards, University career centers, and other directed outreach Managing and updating candidate information across Workday, Interfolio, and internal hiring spreadsheets Building and maintaining a tagged candidate database from past applicant data to enable rapid re-engagement as new roles open. Recruiting Analytics & Tools: Assisting with tracking and reporting recruitment metrics, including time-to-fill, conversion rates, and overall pipeline health Benchmarking sourcing and talent acquisition tools and recommending additions to CSET's recruitment stack Assisting in data collection, analysis, and reporting as needed Recruiting Process Improvement: Auditing the recruiting lifecycle to identify friction points and eliminate manual steps, including helping  incorporate AI tools and automation into workflows where appropriate Helping update and maintain core recruitment assets such as SOPs, FAQs, and CSET's Careers page Handling confidential and sensitive information with discretion Additional Responsibilities: Monitoring trends and developments in AI, ML, biotechnology, and national security policy Upholding CSET’s mission, values, and culture Additional duties as assigned Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Business, Human Resources, International Relations, Security Studies, or a related field; 1 year of professional work experience; experience in HR, people operations, finance, or policy preferred; Comfort working with data in Google Sheets or Microsoft Excel, including filtering, pivot tables, and formulas; Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and sound judgment; Ability to carry on assigned tasks with limited need for supervision; Proficiency with office productivity tools like Google Docs/Sheets, Microsoft Office, etc. Ability to work successfully in a collaborative matrixed/multi-disciplinary environment Motivated, enthusiastic, intellectually curious and self-driven  Alignment with CSET’s mission, values and culture Ability to work in the United States without employer sponsorship Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated interest or involvement in AI safety, technology policy, or national security; Experience using or integrating AI tools into professional workflows; Familiarity with applicant tracking or recruiting platforms such as Workday, Interfolio, or LinkedIn Recruiter; Prior experience supporting a recruiting or talent acquisition function. This position is based in the United States and offers no relocation assistance. This position is not eligible for a specialty-occupation sponsorship and, accordingly, this position requires that all applicants be legally eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship from Georgetown University Application Instructions: Please note that we only consider complete applications, which include: Resume/CV Cover Letter that addresses the following: Why are you interested in CSET and the People Operations Associate position, specifically? For ease of reviewing all submissions, we ask that candidates submit all application materials, including their resume and cover letter, as a single document in Workday. PDF or DOCX formats are accepted. We encourage all candidates to apply, even those unsure whether they meet all the requirements for the role. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Candidates will be expected to work from CSET’s D.C. office at least 2 days per week. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation .  Pay Range   The projected hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $31.50 - $38.50. Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Associate-Director-of-Administration-and-Operations_JR27452": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Administration and Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Associate Director of Administration and Operations serves as the senior administrator responsible for the administrative and operational functions of the Office of Undergraduate Admissions. Reporting directly to the Dean of Admissions and serving as a member of the Office’s leadership team, the Associate Director provides executive-level administrative and operational support to the Dean and Senior Associate Directors while overseeing the systems, processes, personnel, and resources that support the work of the Office. The Associate Director manages and provides oversight for office operations, personnel administration, procurement, facilities coordination, administrative services, records and workflow management, and other operational functions. The position supervises administrative staff, establishes priorities and expectations, develops and implements procedures, coordinates office-wide projects, and identifies opportunities to improve efficiency, consistency, and service. Working with a high degree of independence and professional judgment, the Associate Director anticipates operational needs, resolves administrative challenges, and ensures that day-to-day functions are effectively coordinated across the Office. The Associate Director also serves as a primary liaison between Undergraduate Admissions and University administrative departments, coordinating matters that require collaboration with Human Resources, Finance, Procurement, Facilities, Information Technology, and other campus partners. The position works closely with admissions leadership and staff to ensure that administrative resources and operational processes are aligned with the demands of the annual admissions cycle and evolving departmental priorities. Through this work, the Associate Director plays a critical role in maintaining the administrative infrastructure necessary for a complex, high-volume admissions operation. The position ensures that the Dean, leadership, admissions officers, and administrative staff have the operational support, resources, and processes necessary to carry out the Office’s responsibilities effectively and to advance the University’s undergraduate enrollment priorities. Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Direct the administrative operations and business functions of the Office of Undergraduate Admissions Provide executive-level administrative support to the Dean of Admissions and Senior Associate Directors Manages 2 direct reports and 4 indirect reports Supervise administrative staff and oversee hiring, onboarding, performance management, and professional development Develop, implement, and evaluate administrative policies, procedures, and operational practices Oversee personnel administration, office operations, records management, procurement, facilities coordination, and administrative technology Manage administrative projects and operational initiatives that support departmental priorities Oversee the administrative resources that support recruitment activities, admissions programs, events, and strategic initiatives Serve as the Office's primary liaison with University administrative departments Oversee procurement, contracts, vendor relationships, budget monitoring, and stewardship of administrative resources Evaluate administrative processes and implement improvements that enhance service, efficiency, and compliance. Work Interactions The Associate Director reports directly to the Dean of Admissions and serves as a member of the Office's leadership team. The position works closely with the Dean, Senior Associate Directors, admissions officers, operations staff, and administrative personnel to establish administrative priorities and support departmental initiatives. The Associate Director directly supervises the Administrative Officer/Admissions Support Team Manager and the Assistant Director of Operations, providing leadership, coaching, performance management, and professional development. The position serves as the primary administrative liaison with Human Resources, Finance and Business Services, Procurement, University Information Services, Facilities Management, Payroll, Student Employment, University Events, the Office of the Provost, and other University departments. The Associate Director also works with vendors, alumni volunteers, prospective students, families, counselors, and other partners as needed to support Office operations. Requirements and Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Seven plus years of progressively responsible administrative or operational management experience Demonstrated experience supervising professional and administrative staff. Experience managing office operations, business processes, and administrative services. Excellent organizational, interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and meet competing deadlines. Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain confidentiality. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and enterprise administrative systems. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree strongly preferred Experience in higher education administration, admissions operations, enrollment management, or related academic environments Experience overseeing administrative operations, personnel coordination, or organizational workflow management Familiarity with HR-related administrative processes, staffing coordination, and operational planning Experience supporting high-volume operational environments with multiple functional areas and stakeholders Familiarity with Slate, Workday, Banner, Google Workspace, Microsoft Office applications, or similar operational systems Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $66,783.00 - $126,720.23 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Administrative-Project-Coordinator--Vice-Provost-for-Research_JR27423": {
      "title": "Administrative Project Coordinator, Vice Provost for Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview This position based in the Office of the Provost will provide direct administrative support to the Vice Provost for Research and to the Deputy to the Provost, and will complete additional tasks as assigned.  The individual must be organized, efficient, and able to coordinate multiple projects simultaneously.  S/he must be highly motivated, results-oriented, and pro-active in providing administrative, financial, and research support for the Office. This individual will prepare briefings, compose PowerPoint presentations, edit websites, send broadcast University mailings as needed, schedule, organize and manage meetings, projects, and events, execute related administrative functions, and stand in for the Special Assistant to the Provost in his/her absence.  The position requires superior organizational skills, a capacity to anticipate needs and to pre-emptively address them, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively with colleagues across the university. S/he will work in a team-oriented environment with the goal of ensuring the success of the Provost’s Office business and overall University initiatives. The work performed will be integral to the effective functioning of the Provost’s Office and its ability to implement projects, initiatives, and normal administrative duties throughout Main Campus.   Work Interactions The position will administratively report to the Vice Provost for Research, but will functionally report jointly to the Vice Provost for Research and the Deputy to the Provost, spending time working in each area.  The incumbent will interact closely with senior leaders in the Provost’s Office, and high-level stakeholders internally and externally including deans, faculty members, funding agencies, and others.  Requirements and Qualifications The successful candidate will possess the following qualifications: Superior written and verbal communication skills Outstanding organizational skills Exceptional reliability and work ethic Advanced Word, Excel PowerPoint, and web editing skills A familiarity with GMS an advantage A minimum of 1-3 years’ practical experience working in an administrative role preferable. Bachelor’s degree required. Advanced degree preferred. Experience working with senior leaders in a higher education setting preferable. Experience in managing multiple projects for multiple principals simultaneously.  Experience in working with Confidential Information Budgets/ Organization structures/ HR –related issues. High level of professionalism required. Experience in working on research administration issues and research grants a positive attribute. Experience working with funding agencies, including federal agencies, private foundations, and corporate sponsors, a positive attribute. Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as On-Campus. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $20.16 - $31.30 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Main-Campus/Advising-Dean--Dean-s-Office---Georgetown-University-College-of-Arts---Sciences_JR27453": {
      "title": "Advising Dean, Dean's Office – Georgetown University College of Arts & Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The advising team of the College supports the Dean of the College in carrying out his responsibility for the general effectiveness of the instructional programs of the College, and in carrying out academic policies and regulations. The advising team of the College collectively advise 3700 undergraduates pursuing ~50 majors and ~50 minors in the bachelor of arts and bachelor of science degree programs.   The position serves on a team of professional staff whose time is primarily devoted to academic advising students in the College. The advising dean monitors students' progress toward degrees, arbitrates important academic issues, oversees and approves registration for courses, provides academic guidance, adjudicates and interprets academic regulations of the College, and supports academic orientation to the University.   The position is charged with maintaining the academic files and ensuring the integrity of the academic record for approximately 300 advisees. For those students, the advising dean will review/approve:  transfer credit, study abroad programs, changes to a student’s academic program, and exceptions in the student’s degree audit. Consistent with Georgetown’s commitment to cura personalis, this position, though primarily an academic advisor, supports and advises students on any and all matters which interfere with personal well-being and academic success. The advising dean will make frequent referrals to – and have regular contact with – campus partner offices, and must be well-versed in the services those offices provide.   All advising team staff participate in College Academic Council events, office retreats, New Student Orientation, Parents Weekend and Commencement activities in various roles. Work Interactions This position reports directly to an Associate Dean, and interacts daily with other advisors and two records specialists on the team. At any given time, this position might interact with any of the 3700 students of the College, or any of the main campus faculty who teach them. This position has the authority to and is expected to handle and resolve many delicate and complex conflicts between student and faculty, student and parent, parent and the institution, with all appropriate tact, sensitivity, and a sense of the academic standards to be applied to each such conflict.  The position will also interact with colleagues in partner offices across campus. Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in an academic field appropriate to a college of arts and sciences. 3-5 years’ experience in higher education advising or administration. Demonstrated interest in academic advising. Appreciation for the value of a liberal arts education. An understanding of Georgetown’s Jesuit and Catholic identity. Excellent written and oral communication skills; good listening skills. Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously, meet time-sensitive deadlines, and set priorities.  Strong orientation to detail. A penchant for problem-solving. Ability to work well under pressure and function as a team player. Possess poise, diplomacy and confidence to handle a variety of situations, especially those of a confidential nature and in interactions with faculty, parents and partner offices. Sensitivity to the needs and concerns of a diverse student population. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in an academic field appropriate to a college of arts and sciences. Familiarity with student information systems. Prior teaching, counseling or administrative work.  Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid . Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Cover letter and resume required for consideration Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $47,586.00 - $87,558.13 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
