    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/2115-Wisconsin-Ave-G1-Floor/Director-of-Campus-Accounting_JR26946": {
      "title": "Director of Campus Accounting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview Reporting to the University’s Assistant Controller, the Director of Campus Accounting (“the Director”) is responsible for overseeing and directing the operation of the Campus Accounting Department which includes: financial statements reporting; various audits; general ledger accounting; fund accounting; procard card, and other electronic funds reconciliations; and internal controls and compliance.    The Director is responsible for ensuring campus compliance with generally accepted accounting principles (“GAAP”) and is responsible for the interpretation and application of the University’s financial policies and procedures.  The Director is the principal accounting liaison for all campus accounting activities, including overseeing the completion of the monthly and year-end financial close process and preparation of campus financial statements, supporting schedules and analyses, therefore, it is imperative that the Director have an excellent understanding of GAAP.  In addition, the Director must have an understanding of AICPA audit requirements and complex automated accounting systems    The Director must remain aware of developments that are applicable to the University, assess University exposure, and bring these assessments and action plan proposals to management.  The Director is responsible for reviewing, assessing, implementing, and enforcing the internal controls over financial reporting and ensuring that the policies and procedures are up-to-date, relevant, and complied with.  The Director is responsible for the analysis of financial information through the use of queries, spreadsheets, databases, and other reporting tools for trend analyses, forecasts, and financial ratios.   The Director must possess quality management and leadership skills that will assist the staff to accomplish objectives and direct the department in a way that makes it more cohesive and coherent. The Director must be able to handle complex personnel issues that may arise and the ability to communicate effectively and discipline when necessary.   Work Interactions This is a highly technical position with a far-reaching impact on the University. The Director of Campus Accounting reports to the Assistant Controller within the Office of the CFO of the University but has a wide-ranging scope of relationships both internal and external to the University.   This position requires strong technical accounting and financial expertise, leadership and good judgment that are critical to the department’s success.  The position must develop an atmosphere of teamwork within the department and commit retention and cross training for the benefit of both campus accounting staff and the University in an ever changing environment.  The Director provides leadership to other professionals in the Office of the CFO and works closely with, senior University administrators, departmental professionals and other University staff on a wide variety of financial initiatives.  This position plays a key strategic role in identifying, developing and implementing internal controls, financial standards, policies, and procedures for the entire University.   Requirements and Qualifications ●        Bachelor degree in Accounting or Finance is required  ●        Master degree in Accounting or MBA is desirable ●        Minimum eight to ten years progressive experience in financial accounting, reporting, and audit ●        Experience to include a complex higher educational institution or not-for-profit organization and staff supervision  ●        Experience in other organizations of similar size and complexity may be substituted  ●        CPA required ●        Excellent analytical and written & oral communication skills required, as well as attention to detail.      Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $103,723.00 - $202,778.93 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
    },
    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Law-Center/Recruitment-and-Programming-Coordinator_JR27701-1": {
      "title": "Recruitment and Programming Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Recruitment and Programming Coordinator, Office of Graduate Careers, Georgetown Law – Georgetown University, provides computing, technical, research, clerical and administrative support to the Office of Graduate Careers (OGC) team, including handling logistical and organizational matters and playing a supportive role for all student functions and processes. The range of responsibilities include, but is not limited to, draft and send out OGC’s weekly careers newsletter, organizing and executing career events and programs; maintaining data files; preparing special reports and correspondence; processing financial matters for the team; receiving, screening and responding to email; and other electronic communication; and participating in meetings as requested. Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Event Management: submit room requests, create RSVP links and manage all aspects of OGC’s career related events and programs Symplicity: manage multiple versions of Symplicity, upload students to Symplicity, and create Job Postings and Resume Collections as requested by employers Website and Databases: update OGC website, databases, and resources as needed Financial Responsibilities: assist with drafting OGC’s budget, track receipts and expenses, manage catering arrangements for career programs General: draft and send out weekly Careers Newsletter, manage multiple inboxes, conduct marketing for Externships and the Taxation Interview Program, gather data as requested by the Assistant Dean and communicate with multiple stakeholders including students, faculty, staff and employers. Work Interactions This position reports directly to the Assistant Dean in the Office of Graduate Careers. The position plays a crucial role in supporting the career advisors in OGC. OGC serves the career and professional development needs of the graduate students at Georgetown Law. This staff member is expected to maintain current working knowledge of and be an active participant in all activities and issues undertaken by the Office of Graduate Careers. Requirements and Qualifications High School Diploma and 5 or more years of experience, or equivalent relevant work experience; e.g., each year of relevant work experience may be substituted for each year of education required. College preferred. Familiarity with financial systems, budgeting and accounting; experience in event and meeting planning; experience in support functions; excellent oral and written communications skills and student service orientations; demonstrated interpersonal skills; commitment to working with a diverse student body and faculty; team approach to problem solving Proficiency with Microsoft Office required Familiarity with Google Docs/Forms/Drive, MailChimp, Symplicity, and WordPress preferred Computer savvy Attention to detail is important in all aspects of this job Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University. Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation. Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $21.16 - $35.29 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
