    "https://georgetown.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Georgetown_Admin_Careers/job/Medical-Center/Financial-Grant-Manager_JR27758": {
      "title": "Financial Grant Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGeorgetown University comprises two unique campuses in the nation’s capital. With the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of the historic Georgetown neighborhood, and the Capitol Campus, just minutes from the U.S. Capitol and U.S. Supreme Court, Georgetown University offers rigorous academic programs, a global perspective, and unparalleled opportunities to engage with Washington, D.C. Our community is a close-knit group of remarkable individuals driven by intellectual inquiry, a commitment to social justice, and a shared dedication to making a difference in the world. Requirements Job Overview The Financial Grant Manager, Office of the VP of Finance at Georgetown University Medical Center, supports faculty in the financial and compliance management of externally funded awards, serving as an active liaison between faculty and other university offices. The role provides financial oversight, forecasting, and post-award support for ARPA-H awards, including contracts executed through Other Transaction Agreements (OTAs). Responsibilities include maintaining auditable records for expenditures, cost transfers, procurements, and approved budget modifications. The ideal candidate is highly organized and detail-oriented, communicates effectively, and independently manages competing priorities and deadlines. Because these programs are milestone-driven and subject to evolving sponsor requirements, the successful candidate must learn new systems and funding mechanisms quickly, work with agility, and adapt as program scope, milestones, and reporting expectations change.   Additional duties include, but are not limited to: Prepare monthly financial reports, reconciliations, and early warnings for budget variances, underspend, or cashflow risks. Track commitments, actual expenditures, accruals, forecasts, available balances, and burn rates for sponsored projects. Coordinate financial reporting and invoice reviews across prime, co-lead, sub-performers, and consortium participants. Guide faculty through the financial aspects of sponsor progress reports and determine the need for effort adjustments or prior approval requests. Maintain auditable records supporting cost transfers, procurements, consultant costs, and equipment purchases. Apply formal financial change control and support award modifications with accurate cost impact analyses and budget scenarios. Respond quickly to shifting program priorities, re-scoped milestones, and sponsor-driven redirections, re-forecasting and re-baselining budgets on short turnaround.   Work Interactions The Financial Grant Manager reports directly to the Office of the VP of Finance and currently has no direct reports. This position works closely with other staff members across other administrative roles within the University, to ensure that awards are accurate and in compliance with sponsor and institutional regulations. Furthermore, the Financial Grant Manager maintains a close, day-to-day operational partnership with the Lead Project Manager(s) partners with Program Managers and PIs to integrate cost, schedule, and performance information into program reporting. By facilitating seamless financial administration and ensuring stringent compliance, the work performed by this position directly empowers Georgetown University's overarching mission to advance health, science, and the common good through world-class research.   Requirements and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Five to seven years of progressively responsible experience in a grants management role. Knowledge of a variety of sponsored research funding mechanisms, including federal agencies (NIH, ARPA-H, NSF, DOD, etc.). Expertise with federal funding guidelines (e.g., 2 CFR 200, FAR). Proficiency with financial systems, accounting, and cost accounting standards as they pertain to grants and contracts management. Budgeting experience and a high level of proficiency in Excel. Proficient with software products including Adobe Professional and DocuSign. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, organizational skills, with demonstrated ability to thrive in a fast-paced, rapidly evolving research environment. Demonstrated learning agility: able to master unfamiliar funding mechanisms, sponsor requirements, and financial systems quickly and with minimal supervision. Capacity to establish clear priorities, adapt to changing circumstances, and multi-task quickly and effectively under pressure and against short deadlines C ollegial and collaborative working style, with the ability to build and sustain effective working relationships across faculty, internal university offices, internal and external academic/industrial consortium partners, including acting as a close operational partner to Lead Project Managers and PIs in a fast-paced, milestone-driven environment.   Preferred Qualifications Experience managing complex federal post-award finances, preferably ARPA-H, DARPA, BARDA, or similarly milestone-driven awards. Demonstrated experience with milestone-based payments, multi-year forecasting, consortium or multi-site financial coordination, and sub-performer oversight. Familiarity with Workday. Advanced Excel and financial systems skills, with the ability to build clear budget, burn-rate, variance, and forecast dashboards. T rack record of adapting financial processes and reporting tools to accommodate mid-stream changes in program scope, consortium composition, or sponsor reporting requirements.   Work Mode Designation This position has been designated as Hybrid. Please note that work mode designations are regularly reviewed in order to meet the evolving needs of the University.  Such review may necessitate a change to a position’s mode of work designation. Complete details about Georgetown University’s mode of work designations for staff positions can be found on the Department of Human Resources website: https://hr.georgetown.edu/mode-of-work-designation . Pay Range: The projected salary or hourly pay range for this position which represents the full range of anticipated compensation is: $54,616.00 - $100,493.33 Compensation is determined by a number of factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s individual qualifications, experience, education, skills, and certifications, as well as the University’s business needs and external factors. Current Georgetown Employees: If you currently work at Georgetown University, please exit this website and login to GMS ( gms.georgetown.edu ) using your Net ID and password. Then select the Career worklet on your GMS Home dashboard to view Jobs at Georgetown. Submission Guidelines: Please note that in order to be considered an applicant for any position at Georgetown University you must submit a resume for each position of interest for which you believe you are qualified. Documents are not kept on file for future positions. Need Assistance: If you are a qualified individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodations for any part of the application and hiring process, please visit the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance website for general information about requesting accommodations , as well as information about requesting accommodations specifically for applicants . You also can also contact the Office for Equal Opportunity Compliance at (202) 687-4798 or oeoc@georgetown.edu . Need some assistance with the application process? Please call 202-687-2500. For more information about the suite of benefits, professional development and community involvement opportunities that make up Georgetown's commitment to its employees, please visit the Georgetown Works website . EEO Statement: GU is an Equal Opportunity Employer . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply, and will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, citizenship, color, disability, family responsibilities, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, matriculation, national origin, race, religion, personal appearance, political affiliation, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law . Benefits: Georgetown University offers a comprehensive and competitive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance, retirement savings, tuition assistance, work-life balance benefits, employee discounts and an array of voluntary insurance options. You can learn more about benefits and eligibility on the Department of Human Resources website ."
